01:09:07,012 --> 01:09:09,681
<i>Vipera Evanesca!</i>

731
01:09:16,396 --> 01:09:18,732
What were you playing?

732
01:09:31,537 --> 01:09:34,248
You speak Parseltongue!
Why hadn't you told us?

733
01:09:34,414 --> 01:09:36,667
- What?
- You can talk to the vipers.

734
01:09:36,834 --> 01:09:42,130
I already know. I once threw a python at him
on top of my cousin Dudley, by accident.

735
01:09:42,297 --> 01:09:46,260
Once, but so what? I bet
because many people here can do it.

736
01:09:46,426 --> 01:09:50,222
No, they can't.
It's not a very common gift, Harry.

737
01:09:50,722 --> 01:09:52,432
This is bad.

738
01:09:52,599 --> 01:09:56,311
What is bad? If I don't tell him
To the viper not to attack Justin...

739
01:09:56,478 --> 01:09:59,982
- Ah, that's what you told him.
- You were present. You heard me.

740
01:10:00,148 --> 01:10:04,069
I heard you speaking Parseltongue.
The tongue of snakes.

741
01:10:04,236 --> 01:10:07,114
Did I speak in another language?

742
01:10:08,156 --> 01:10:10,576
But I didn't realize...

743
01:10:10,742 --> 01:10:13,495
How can I speak another language
without knowing what I can?

744
01:10:13,662 --> 01:10:17,708
I don't know, but it seemed like you were
encouraging the viper.

745
01:10:17,875 --> 01:10:19,585
Harry, listen to me.

746
01:10:19,960 --> 01:10:22,838
The symbol of Slytherin House
It's the snake.

747
01:10:23,005 --> 01:10:27,551
Salazar Slytherin was a Parseltongue speaker,
I could talk to snakes.

748
01:10:27,801 --> 01:10:28,802
Exactly.

749
01:10:28,969 --> 01:10:32,347
Now the whole school is going to think
that you are his great-great-grandson.

750
01:10:32,514 --> 01:10:34,516
But I'm not!

751
01:10:37,269 --> 01:10:39,187
I can't be.

752
01:10:40,314 --> 01:10:42,357
He lived a thousand years ago.

753
01:10:42,524 --> 01:10:45,777
Given what we know, yes you can be.

754
01:11:15,849 --> 01:11:18,226
See you later in the common room.

755
01:11:34,660 --> 01:11:38,914
<i>I want blood!</i>

756
01:11:41,833 --> 01:11:46,838
<i>Everyone must die!</i>

757
01:11:47,381 --> 01:11:49,383
<i>Kill!</i>

758
01:11:50,050 --> 01:11:52,177
<i>Kill!</i>

759
01:11:52,928 --> 01:11:55,222
<i>Kill!</i>

760
01:11:55,555 --> 01:11:59,643
<i>Time to kill!</i>

761
01:12:33,844 --> 01:12:35,762
with hands
in the dough.

762
01:12:35,929 --> 01:12:37,889
This time I will
get expelled

763
01:12:38,390 --> 01:12:40,892
You'll see.

764
01:12:41,059 --> 01:12:45,272
No, Mr. Filch,
he doesn't understand!

765
01:13:12,049 --> 01:13:13,967
Teacher...

766
01:13:14,134 --> 01:13:15,510
...I swear I didn't go.

767
01:13:15,677 --> 01:13:18,930
This is out
of my control, Potter.

768
01:13:28,565 --> 01:13:31,234
Professor Dumbledore
will be waiting for you.

769
01:13:40,160 --> 01:13:42,746
Lemon sorbet!

770
01:14:16,696 --> 01:14:18,824
Professor Dumbledore?

771
01:14:35,298 --> 01:14:38,009
Can't you get it out of your head?

772
01:14:40,887 --> 01:14:45,392
It's just that I wonder
If you sent me to the right House.

773
01:14:45,559 --> 01:14:51,064
Yes. It was particularly
difficult to assign you.

774
01:14:51,231 --> 01:14:54,734
But I don't take it back
what I said last year.

775
01:14:54,901 --> 01:14:58,321
You would have done well in Slytherin.

776
01:14:58,488 --> 01:14:59,823
You are wrong.

777
01:15:29,102 --> 01:15:30,520
Harry?

778
01:15:30,896 --> 01:15:33,106
Professor!

779
01:15:33,273 --> 01:15:37,110
Your bird...
I couldn't do anything!

780
01:15:37,694 --> 01:15:40,989
- It caught fire suddenly!
- And it was time, too.

781
01:15:41,865 --> 01:15:44,159
He had been looking very bad for days.

782
01:15:44,326 --> 01:15:46,369
Too bad you saw it in one day
burning

783
01:15:48,288 --> 01:15:51,499
Fawkes is a phoenix, Harry.

784
01:15:51,666 --> 01:15:55,045
They catch fire when it reaches them
the moment of dying...

785
01:15:55,212 --> 01:15:57,297
...and then they are reborn...

786
01:15:57,464 --> 01:16:00,508
...from his ashes.

787
01:16:08,934 --> 01:16:11,561
The phoenixes are
some fascinating creatures.

788
01:16:11,978 --> 01:16:15,899
They can carry loads
immensely heavy...

789
01:16:16,066 --> 01:16:18,902
...and her tears have
healing powers.

790
01:16:21,488 --> 01:16:24,574
Professor Dumbledore, sir!
Wait, listen!

791
01:16:25,533 --> 01:16:27,661
It wasn't Harry.

792
01:16:28,828 --> 01:16:31,706
I would swear before
the Ministry of Magic.

793
01:16:33,166 --> 01:16:35,085
Calm down.

794
01:16:35,835 --> 01:16:37,796
I don't believe...

795
01:16:37,963 --> 01:16:41,299
- ...that Harry has attacked anyone.
- Of course not.

796
01:16:45,178 --> 01:16:47,806
True. Well, I...

797
01:16:47,973 --> 01:16:51,101
- I'll wait outside, then.
- Yes.

798
01:16:54,771 --> 01:16:58,441
- You don't think it was me, professor?
- No, Harry.

799
01:16:58,608 --> 01:17:01,111
I don't think it was you.

800
01:17:02,153 --> 01:17:03,947
But I need to ask you:

801
01:17:04,531 --> 01:17:08,618
Is there something you want to tell me?

802
01:17:15,041 --> 01:17:17,002
No, sir.

803
01:17:17,168 --> 01:17:18,670
Nothing.

804
01:17:21,673 --> 01:17:23,842
Very well, then.

805
01:17:24,009 --> 01:17:25,802
You can go.

806
01:18:03,757 --> 01:18:07,260
Everything is ready. There's just something missing
of their future identities.

807
01:18:07,427 --> 01:18:09,179
Crabbe and Goyle.

808
01:18:09,346 --> 01:18:12,098
We must also ensure
that Crabbe and Goyle...

809
01:18:12,265 --> 01:18:15,518
...don't burst into the room
when we're with Malfoy.

810
01:18:15,852 --> 01:18:18,563
- How?
- I already planned everything.

811
01:18:18,730 --> 01:18:21,274
I filled these with a potion
to sleep.

812
01:18:21,441 --> 01:18:24,235
Simple but powerful.

813
01:18:24,444 --> 01:18:26,613
Since they are asleep...

814
01:18:26,780 --> 01:18:29,991
...hide them in the closet,
remove some hairs...

815
01:18:30,158 --> 01:18:32,077
...and put on your uniforms.

816
01:18:32,243 --> 01:18:35,497
- Who will you rip it off from?
- I already have mine.

817
01:18:35,663 --> 01:18:38,875
They're by Millicent Bulstrode. Slytherin.

818
01:18:39,042 --> 01:18:41,211
I removed these from his tunic.

819
01:18:41,378 --> 01:18:43,963
I'll see how it goes
polyjuice potion.

820
01:18:44,130 --> 01:18:46,883
Make Crabbe
and Goyle find these.

821
01:18:58,978 --> 01:19:01,356
Maybe I should do it.

822
01:19:01,523 --> 01:19:03,608
Yes, true.

823
01:19:05,819 --> 01:19:07,153
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

824
01:19:17,789 --> 01:19:19,416
Great!

825
01:19:42,522 --> 01:19:44,357
How stupid are they?

826
01:19:44,524 --> 01:19:46,526
Come, let's go get them.

827
01:19:49,195 --> 01:19:53,199
We have an hour before we return
to become us.

828
01:20:01,374 --> 01:20:03,334
Add the hairs.

829
01:20:07,881 --> 01:20:09,591
Essence of Crabbe.

830
01:20:09,757 --> 01:20:11,676
Health.

831
01:20:20,393 --> 01:20:22,812
I think I'm going to vomit!

832
01:20:25,732 --> 01:20:27,567
Me too.

833
01:21:12,445 --> 01:21:14,155
Harry?

834
01:21:14,614 --> 01:21:16,199
Ron!

835
01:21:16,950 --> 01:21:19,118
Damn it!

836
01:21:19,911 --> 01:21:22,163
Our voices remain the same.

837
01:21:22,330 --> 01:21:24,123
You need to sound more like Crabbe.

838
01:21:25,291 --> 01:21:27,585
- Damn!
- Excellent.

839
01:21:27,919 --> 01:21:30,421
But where is Hermione?

840
01:21:30,588 --> 01:21:33,591
I think I'm not going to go.
Go without me!

841
01:21:33,758 --> 01:21:35,468
Hermione, are you okay?

842
01:21:35,635 --> 01:21:38,471
Go away! They are wasting their time!

843
01:21:40,515 --> 01:21:42,183
Let's go!

844
01:21:45,687 --> 01:21:49,065
The Slytherin common room is this way.

845
01:21:52,026 --> 01:21:54,487
Excuse me.

846
01:21:56,322 --> 01:21:58,241
What are you doing...?

847
01:21:58,408 --> 01:22:00,493
I mean, what are you doing here?

848
01:22:02,370 --> 01:22:05,123
I am a school prefect.

849
01:22:05,290 --> 01:22:09,752
You, on the other hand, should not
wandering through the corridors.

850
01:22:10,336 --> 01:22:12,171
What are they called?

851
01:22:12,338 --> 01:22:16,342
- I am...
- Crabbe, Goyle! Where were they?

852
01:22:16,509 --> 01:22:19,512
Gorging
in the great hall until now?

853
01:22:21,014 --> 01:22:23,349
Why are you wearing glasses?

854
01:22:24,183 --> 01:22:27,020
- They are for reading.
- Read?

855
01:22:28,187 --> 01:22:30,481
Do you know how to read?

856
01:22:33,359 --> 01:22:35,445
And what are you doing here, Weasley?

857
01:22:35,612 --> 01:22:37,655
Don't be insolent, Malfoy.

858
01:22:46,414 --> 01:22:48,416
Well, sit down.

859
01:22:51,210 --> 01:22:55,048
It is not obvious that the Weasleys are blood
clean by his behavior.

860
01:22:55,298 --> 01:22:59,135
They are a shame
for magicians. All of them.

861
01:22:59,969 --> 01:23:02,221
What do you have, Crabbe?

862
01:23:04,474 --> 01:23:06,225
Stomach pain.

863
01:23:08,227 --> 01:23:13,066
I'm surprised the Prophet hasn't
made a report about these attacks.

864
01:23:13,232 --> 01:23:15,693
Dumbledore must want to hide it.

865
01:23:15,943 --> 01:23:18,363
Dad says Dumbledore
It's the worst...

866
01:23:18,529 --> 01:23:22,325
- ...what has happened to this place.
- You're wrong!

867
01:23:29,791 --> 01:23:31,000
How?

868
01:23:31,167 --> 01:23:34,837
Do you think there is someone worse
what Dumbledore?

869
01:23:35,004 --> 01:23:37,423
Yes? Do you think so?

870
01:23:37,924 --> 01:23:39,801
Harry Potter?

871
01:23:46,391 --> 01:23:47,767
Very good, Goyle.

872
01:23:47,934 --> 01:23:49,519
You are absolutely right.

873
01:23:50,144 --> 01:23:52,021
"Saint Potter."

874
01:23:53,022 --> 01:23:55,775
And do people think that he really
Is he the heir of Slytherin?

875
01:23:59,570 --> 01:24:02,156
Do you have any idea who
is behind this?

876
01:24:02,323 --> 01:24:06,035
You know I don't have it, Goyle.
I told you yesterday.

877
01:24:06,994 --> 01:24:09,539
How many times do I have it for you
what to say?

878
01:24:10,498 --> 01:24:12,375
Is this yours?

879
01:24:16,796 --> 01:24:19,215
But my dad did tell me this:

880
01:24:19,590 --> 01:24:22,468
50 years ago since
that the Chamber was opened.

881
01:24:22,635 --> 01:24:27,056
He didn't tell me who it was.
Only they expelled him.

882
01:24:27,306 --> 01:24:31,978
The last time they opened the Chamber
a mudblood died.

883
01:24:32,145 --> 01:24:36,482
So it's a matter of time
before another dies this time.

884
01:24:37,066 --> 01:24:38,901
myself...

885
01:24:39,068 --> 01:24:41,237
...I hope it's Granger.

886
01:24:41,404 --> 01:24:43,614
What's wrong with you two?

887
01:24:43,781 --> 01:24:46,284
They are very rare.

888
01:24:46,451 --> 01:24:48,661
It's your stomach ache.

889
01:24:48,828 --> 01:24:50,872
Calm down.

890
01:24:55,042 --> 01:24:57,044
Scar!

891
01:25:00,673 --> 01:25:02,091
Hair!

892
01:25:08,264 --> 01:25:10,641
Where are they going?

893
01:25:13,644 --> 01:25:14,896
Just barely!

894
01:25:15,062 --> 01:25:17,523
Get out! We have a lot to tell you.

895
01:25:17,690 --> 01:25:19,525
Go away!

896
01:25:20,026 --> 01:25:23,946
Wait until you see it! It's horrible!

897
01:25:25,865 --> 01:25:27,658
Hermione?

898
01:25:27,825 --> 01:25:29,452
Are you okay?

899
01:25:31,496 --> 01:25:33,247
Do you remember that I told you...

900
01:25:33,414 --> 01:25:36,584
...that the potion was just
for human transformations?

901
01:25:36,751 --> 01:25:40,880
The hair that Millicent had
In his tunic they were cat-like.

902
01:25:43,257 --> 01:25:44,842
Look what face I have.

903
01:25:45,968 --> 01:25:48,387
Look at that tail!

904
01:25:54,977 --> 01:25:56,395
Have you spoken to Hermione?

905
01:25:56,562 --> 01:25:59,148
Will leave the hospital
in a few days...

906
01:25:59,315 --> 01:26:02,109
...when I stop spitting
hairballs.

907
01:26:06,906 --> 01:26:08,658
What is this?

908
01:26:13,246 --> 01:26:14,288
Yuck!

909
01:26:14,455 --> 01:26:17,250
It seems that Moaning Myrtle
flooded the bathroom.

910
01:26:33,474 --> 01:26:37,603
- Did they come to throw something else at me?
- Why would I throw something at you?

911
01:26:38,062 --> 01:26:42,108
Don't ask me. I was here
doing my thing...

912
01:26:42,275 --> 01:26:45,945
...and someone thought it was funny
throw a book at me.

913
01:26:46,112 --> 01:26:49,031
But no one can hurt you
throwing something at you.

914
01:26:49,198 --> 01:26:51,617
I mean, it passes through you and that's it.

915
01:26:52,618 --> 01:26:57,039
Yes, of course! You have to add books
to Myrtle because she's not sorry!

916
01:26:57,206 --> 01:26:59,792
10 points if you cross him
the stomach!

917
01:26:59,959 --> 01:27:03,462
50 points if you put it through the head!

918
01:27:03,963 --> 01:27:08,426
-Who gave it to you?
- Don't know. I didn't see it.

919
01:27:08,759 --> 01:27:12,972
I was sitting in the siphon,
thinking about death...

920
01:27:13,180 --> 01:27:16,893
...and it fell on my head.

921
01:27:47,006 --> 01:27:49,508
"Tom Marvolo Riddle."

922
01:28:19,372 --> 01:28:21,707
My name is...

923
01:28:21,874 --> 01:28:24,835
...Harry...

924
01:28:26,420 --> 01:28:28,547
...Potter.

925
01:28:32,426 --> 01:28:37,390
Hello Harry Potter,
My name is Tom Riddle.

926
01:28:41,811 --> 01:28:46,983
Do you know anything about...

927
01:28:47,775 --> 01:28:54,490
...from the Chamber of Secrets?

928
01:28:57,493 --> 01:28:59,078
<i>Yes</i>

929
01:29:04,583 --> 01:29:06,544
Do I...

930
01:29:07,753 --> 01:29:10,089
...can you say?

931
01:29:18,264 --> 01:29:21,767
But I can teach you

932
01:29:24,520 --> 01:29:28,107
let me take you back in time
50 years ago

933
01:29:32,278 --> 01:29:34,530
June 13

934
01:30:12,318 --> 01:30:15,780
Excuse me. can you tell me
what is happening here?

935
01:30:19,200 --> 01:30:21,535
Are you Tom Riddle?

936
01:30:21,702 --> 01:30:23,496
Hello, can you hear me?

937
01:30:44,100 --> 01:30:45,851
Riddle!

938
01:30:46,435 --> 01:30:47,978
Come.

939
01:30:48,145 --> 01:30:50,147
Professor Dumbledore.

940
01:30:52,316 --> 01:30:54,485
Dumbledore.

941
01:30:55,778 --> 01:30:59,240
It's not wise to hang around
So late, Tom.

942
01:30:59,406 --> 01:31:02,743
Yes, professor. I guess...

943
01:31:02,910 --> 01:31:05,121
I had to see if the rumors
They were true.

944
01:31:05,704 --> 01:31:08,582
I'm afraid they are, Tom.

945
01:31:08,749 --> 01:31:11,627
The one at school too?
I have nowhere to go.

946
01:31:11,794 --> 01:31:14,630
They are not capable
to close Hogwarts, right?

947
01:31:14,797 --> 01:31:17,341
I understand, Tom, but I'm afraid...

948
01:31:18,092 --> 01:31:21,053
...that the director maybe
have no choice.

949
01:31:21,220 --> 01:31:25,724
Lord, if the crimes would stop,
If they caught the person responsible...

950
01:31:27,977 --> 01:31:30,062
Is there something...

951
01:31:31,021 --> 01:31:33,023
...what do you want to tell me?

952
01:31:34,233 --> 01:31:36,735
No, sir. Nothing.

953
01:31:43,534 --> 01:31:46,579
Very well, then. You can go.

954
01:31:46,745 --> 01:31:48,581
Good evening, sir.

955
01:32:24,742 --> 01:32:27,620
- Let's get out of here.
- Good night, Hagrid.

956
01:32:27,953 --> 01:32:32,291
I'm going to have to accuse you, Hagrid.
I don't think he killed on purpose...

957
01:32:32,458 --> 01:32:34,793
You can't! You just don't understand!

958
01:32:34,960 --> 01:32:38,088
The dead woman's parents are coming.
Hogwarts needs to make sure...

959
01:32:38,255 --> 01:32:41,133
...that the thing dies
who killed his daughter.

960
01:32:41,425 --> 01:32:44,553
Aragog has never killed
to nobody. Never!

961
01:32:44,845 --> 01:32:47,014
Monsters are not
good pets.

962
01:32:47,181 --> 01:32:48,807
- Move aside.
- No!

963
01:32:48,974 --> 01:32:50,976
- Move over, Hagrid!
- No!

964
01:32:51,143 --> 01:32:52,770
<i>Cistem Aperio!</i>

965
01:32:59,693 --> 01:33:02,071
<i>Arania Exumai!</i>

966
01:33:02,947 --> 01:33:04,406
Aragog!

967
01:33:04,573 --> 01:33:05,824
Aragog!

968
01:33:06,325 --> 01:33:07,743
I can't leave
let you go

969
01:33:08,285 --> 01:33:11,580
They are going to take your wand
for this. They are going to expel you.

970
01:33:14,124 --> 01:33:16,001
Hagrid!

971
01:33:46,031 --> 01:33:50,160
It was Hagrid. Hagrid opened the Chamber
of the Secrets 50 years ago.

972
01:33:50,327 --> 01:33:53,289
It can't be Hagrid.
It just can't be.

973
01:33:53,455 --> 01:33:57,543
We don't know Tom Riddle.
He seems like a lowly snitch to me.

974
01:33:57,710 --> 01:34:01,213
The monster killed someone.
What would we have done?

975
01:34:01,505 --> 01:34:05,467
Hagrid is our friend.
Why don't we go and ask him?

976
01:34:05,676 --> 01:34:08,345
What a lively visit:
«Hello, Hagrid, Tell us...

977
01:34:08,512 --> 01:34:12,349
...did you recently say something crazy?
and hairy in the castle?

978
01:34:12,516 --> 01:34:15,728
Crazy and hairy?
Are they talking about me?

979
01:34:16,061 --> 01:34:17,062
No.

980
01:34:21,567 --> 01:34:23,193
What do you bring there?

981
01:34:23,610 --> 01:34:28,198
Carnivorous slug repellent.
For the mandrakes, you know.

