01:56:22,720 --> 01:56:25,514
Takes the glory of what
other magicians did!

1228
01:56:25,681 --> 01:56:27,600
Can you do something?

1229
01:56:27,767 --> 01:56:32,521
Yes, since you say so. I'm good
for memory spells.

1230
01:56:32,688 --> 01:56:35,191
If not, the other magicians
they would have talked...

1231
01:56:35,358 --> 01:56:38,444
...and I would never have sold
another book.

1232
01:56:38,611 --> 01:56:44,367
The truth is, I'm going to have them!
than to do the same to you!

1233
01:56:44,867 --> 01:56:47,620
Don't even think about it.

1234
01:56:58,506 --> 01:56:59,924
Who's there?

1235
01:57:02,385 --> 01:57:04,428
Hello, Harry.

1236
01:57:05,346 --> 01:57:10,518
- What do you want?
-Ask you how you died.

1237
01:57:12,895 --> 01:57:15,314
It was horrible!

1238
01:57:15,481 --> 01:57:19,193
It happened here, in this same cubicle.

1239
01:57:19,360 --> 01:57:23,406
I hid because Olive Hornby
He was making fun of my glasses.

1240
01:57:23,572 --> 01:57:28,452
I was crying and then
I heard someone come in.

1241
01:57:28,619 --> 01:57:34,959
-Who was it, Myrtle?
- Don't know! I was afflicted!

1242
01:57:36,293 --> 01:57:39,672
But he said something funny,
in an invented language.

1243
01:57:39,839 --> 01:57:46,178
I realized it was a boy,
so I opened it to tell him to leave...

1244
01:57:47,388 --> 01:57:52,226
- ...and I died.
- Just like that? As?

1245
01:57:52,393 --> 01:57:56,897
I only remember seeing a couple.
with huge yellow eyes.

1246
01:57:57,064 --> 01:58:00,901
There, next to that sink.

1247
01:58:26,010 --> 01:58:28,012
Here it is.

1248
01:58:28,929 --> 01:58:33,726
This is it, Ron. I think this is the entrance
to the Chamber of Secrets.

1249
01:58:35,728 --> 01:58:40,608
Say something. Harry,
say something in Parseltongue.

1250
01:59:32,117 --> 01:59:36,247
Excellent, Harry. Good job!
Well, I'm going to...

1251
01:59:36,413 --> 01:59:38,666
There is no need
that I stay!

1252
01:59:39,250 --> 01:59:41,168
Yes, there is!

1253
01:59:42,962 --> 01:59:46,090
- You first.
- But what good will it do?

1254
01:59:46,257 --> 01:59:47,591
Better you than us.

1255
01:59:48,759 --> 01:59:51,720
But... Obviously, yes.

1256
01:59:55,975 --> 01:59:58,727
Don't you want to try it first?

1257
02:00:05,526 --> 02:00:08,779
It's extremely dirty down here.

1258
02:00:09,238 --> 02:00:13,784
- Good. Let's go.
- Hey, Harry?

1259
02:00:14,159 --> 02:00:19,123
If you die down there,
We can share my toilet.

1260
02:00:21,625 --> 02:00:23,627
Thanks, Myrtle.

1261
02:00:52,698 --> 02:00:57,912
Remember. If there are signs of movement,
close your eyes right away.

1262
02:00:58,829 --> 02:01:00,497
Go ahead.

1263
02:01:04,209 --> 02:01:05,544
Over here.

1264
02:01:12,593 --> 02:01:17,848
- What is this?
- It looks like a snake.

1265
02:01:18,015 --> 02:01:21,685
- It's the skin of a snake.
- Wow!

1266
02:01:21,852 --> 02:01:27,650
The thing that took off that skin must
measuring about 20 meters! Or more!

1267
02:01:29,526 --> 02:01:32,529
He has the heart of a lion.

1268
02:01:36,200 --> 02:01:40,871
The adventure ends here, guys.
But don't worry.

1269
02:01:42,831 --> 02:01:48,295
The world will know the story. will know
that I was late to save the girl...

1270
02:01:48,629 --> 02:01:52,132
...and how you lost your reason...

1271
02:01:52,299 --> 02:01:55,260
...when seeing his destroyed corpse.

1272
02:01:56,136 --> 02:01:57,554
So...

1273
02:01:58,722 --> 02:02:01,058
...you first, Mr. Potter.

1274
02:02:01,266 --> 02:02:04,436
Say goodbye to your memories.

1275
02:02:06,522 --> 02:02:08,440
<i>Obliviate!</i>

1276
02:02:42,391 --> 02:02:45,519
- Ron! Ron, are you okay?
- Perfectly!

1277
02:02:49,273 --> 02:02:51,025
Hello.

1278
02:02:51,692 --> 02:02:53,527
And you, who are you?

1279
02:02:54,903 --> 02:02:57,573
-Ron Weasley.
- Really?

1280
02:02:57,740 --> 02:03:00,617
And who am I?

1281
02:03:02,369 --> 02:03:06,665
The spell backfired!
He has no idea who he is!

1282
02:03:06,999 --> 02:03:11,503
What a strange place, right?

1283
02:03:11,670 --> 02:03:13,797
Do you live here?

1284
02:03:14,506 --> 02:03:17,051
- No.
- Really?

1285
02:03:21,638 --> 02:03:23,432
- What do I do?
- Wait here...

1286
02:03:23,599 --> 02:03:26,518
...and remove stones to
that we can return.

1287
02:03:26,685 --> 02:03:30,355
- I'm going to go get Ginny.
- Alright.

1288
02:05:03,574 --> 02:05:07,452
Ginny. Ginny, please!
Don't be dead! Wake up, wake up!

1289
02:05:07,953 --> 02:05:10,080
Please wake up!

1290
02:05:10,330 --> 02:05:12,457
He's not going to wake up.

1291
02:05:17,921 --> 02:05:22,259
Tom. Tom Riddle.
How is he not going to wake up?

1292
02:05:22,426 --> 02:05:25,804
- It's not...
- She's still alive, but barely.

1293
02:05:26,805 --> 02:05:29,099
- Are you a ghost?
- I am a memory...

1294
02:05:29,266 --> 02:05:31,685
...preserved in a diary for 50 years.

1295
02:05:34,354 --> 02:05:39,568
It's very cold. Ginny, you can't
be dead Wake up.

1296
02:05:39,735 --> 02:05:42,112
You have to help me.
There is a basilisk.

1297
02:05:42,279 --> 02:05:44,907
He will only come if they call him.

1298
02:05:47,701 --> 02:05:50,495
- Give me my wand, Tom.
- You're not going to need it.

1299
02:05:51,580 --> 02:05:54,958
- We have to go, we have to save her!
- I'm afraid I can't.

1300
02:05:55,125 --> 02:05:59,171
You see, the weaker Ginny gets,
the more I get stronger.

1301
02:06:00,547 --> 02:06:05,052
Yes, Harry. Ginny Weasley was the
who opened the Chamber of Secrets.

1302
02:06:05,219 --> 02:06:07,554
No. He couldn't. I wouldn't do that.

1303
02:06:07,721 --> 02:06:10,933
Ginny ordered the basilisk
attack the mudbloods.

1304
02:06:11,099 --> 02:06:13,518
She wrote the messages on the walls.

1305
02:06:13,685 --> 02:06:16,980
- But why?
- Because I told him.

1306
02:06:17,147 --> 02:06:22,152
You'll see that I can be very persuasive.
Although she didn't know what she was doing.

1307
02:06:22,319 --> 02:06:25,656
I was, let's say,
in a kind of trance.

1308
02:06:26,156 --> 02:06:28,659
The power of the diary began to scare her...

1309
02:06:28,825 --> 02:06:31,203
...and tried to get rid
of him in the girls' bathroom.

1310
02:06:31,370 --> 02:06:35,749
And then who
found it, but you?

1311
02:06:35,916 --> 02:06:39,002
Just the person who most
I wanted to know.

1312
02:06:39,628 --> 02:06:41,672
And why did you want to meet me?

1313
02:06:42,089 --> 02:06:45,467
I needed to talk to you, meet you,
if it were possible.

1314
02:06:45,634 --> 02:06:48,887
I decided to show you my capture
of Hagrid's clumsy...

1315
02:06:49,054 --> 02:06:52,224
- ...to gain your trust.
-Hagrid is my friend!

1316
02:06:53,183 --> 02:06:57,771
- And you set a trap for him, right?
- It was my word against his.

1317
02:06:57,938 --> 02:07:01,191
Only Dumbledore believed
that he was innocent.

1318
02:07:01,358 --> 02:07:03,527
Dumbledore saw what you were like.

1319
02:07:03,694 --> 02:07:07,197
After that it never took me away
the eyes above.

1320
02:07:07,364 --> 02:07:10,659
I knew it wasn't safe
reopen the Chamber...

1321
02:07:10,826 --> 02:07:12,661
...so I decided to leave a diary...

1322
02:07:12,828 --> 02:07:14,913
...preserving my person
at 16 years old...

1323
02:07:15,080 --> 02:07:17,791
...so that one day he would guide someone...

1324
02:07:17,958 --> 02:07:20,752
...to finish the noble work
by Salazar Slytherin.

1325
02:07:20,919 --> 02:07:23,213
Well you haven't finished it this time.

1326
02:07:23,380 --> 02:07:26,341
In a few hours, the potion
of mandrake will be ready...

1327
02:07:26,508 --> 02:07:29,219
...and all the petrified will heal.

1328
02:07:29,636 --> 02:07:34,891
Didn't I tell you? Kill the mudbloods
I don't care anymore.

1329
02:07:35,142 --> 02:07:39,896
For many months now,
My new target has been you.

1330
02:07:41,398 --> 02:07:44,985
How come a baby
without any extraordinary magical talent...

1331
02:07:45,152 --> 02:07:47,821
...was able to defeat the greatest wizard
of all time?

1332
02:07:48,155 --> 02:07:51,074
how did you escape
with only one scar...

1333
02:07:51,241 --> 02:07:53,660
...while Lord Voldemort
lost his powers?

1334
02:07:53,827 --> 02:07:57,998
What does that matter to you?
Voldemort came after you.

1335
02:07:58,165 --> 02:08:04,629
Voldemort is my past
my present and my future.

1336
02:08:20,771 --> 02:08:23,774
I AM LORD VOLDEMORT

1337
02:08:25,067 --> 02:08:28,487
You. You are the heir of Slytherin.

1338
02:08:31,656 --> 02:08:35,285
- You are Voldemort.
- You certainly didn't believe...

1339
02:08:35,452 --> 02:08:39,956
...who was going to keep the dirty name
from my muggle father.

1340
02:08:40,123 --> 02:08:44,294
No. I made a new name for myself, a name
who knew that one day all the wizards...

1341
02:08:44,461 --> 02:08:48,632
...they would be afraid to say, when it came
to be the greatest magician in the world!

1342
02:08:48,799 --> 02:08:51,968
Albus Dumbledore is the wizard
biggest in the world!

1343
02:08:52,135 --> 02:08:55,555
Dumbledore has been expelled
of the castle thanks to my simple memory.

1344
02:08:55,722 --> 02:09:00,811
It won't disappear as long as
Those of us who remain are faithful to him.

1345
02:09:07,192 --> 02:09:08,193
Fawkes?

1346
02:09:24,501 --> 02:09:28,046
Is that what Dumbledore tells you?
to his great defender?

1347
02:09:28,213 --> 02:09:31,925
A bird and an old hat.

1348
02:09:45,188 --> 02:09:49,734
Let's face the powers of Lord Voldemort,
heir of Salazar Slytherin...

1349
02:09:49,901 --> 02:09:53,947
...against the famous Harry Potter.

1350
02:10:07,252 --> 02:10:11,590
'Talking Arsel won't save you!
1
He only obeys me!

1351
02:10:41,786 --> 02:10:43,371
Nope!

1352
02:10:43,788 --> 02:10:48,293
Maybe your bird has blinded
to the basilisk, but he can still hear you!

1353
02:12:30,312 --> 02:12:33,607
Yes, Potter. The process
It's almost over.

1354
02:12:33,773 --> 02:12:38,695
In a few minutes Ginny Weasley will die
and I will stop being a memory.

1355
02:12:38,862 --> 02:12:41,531
Lord Voldemort will return...

1356
02:12:41,865 --> 02:12:46,077
...full...of...life.

1357
02:12:46,828 --> 02:12:48,204
Ginny?

1358
02:15:04,549 --> 02:15:06,176
It's amazing, isn't it?

1359
02:15:06,342 --> 02:15:10,346
How quickly the poison
penetrates the body.

1360
02:15:10,513 --> 02:15:13,183
You have little more left
of one minute of life.

1361
02:15:13,516 --> 02:15:17,520
You will soon be with
your dear mudblood mother.

1362
02:15:22,525 --> 02:15:26,196
It's funny, the damage that a fool
little book can cause...

1363
02:15:26,362 --> 02:15:31,409
...especially in hands
of a silly little girl.

1364
02:15:34,287 --> 02:15:36,122
What are you doing?

1365
02:15:38,917 --> 02:15:41,044
Stop! No!

1366
02:16:39,352 --> 02:16:43,314
It was me. But I swear
That wasn't on purpose!

1367
02:16:43,481 --> 02:16:46,985
Riddle forced me, and...

1368
02:16:47,527 --> 02:16:50,154
Harry, you're hurt!

1369
02:16:50,530 --> 02:16:52,031
Don't worry.

1370
02:16:52,198 --> 02:16:55,827
Ginny, you need to go.

1371
02:16:55,994 --> 02:16:59,289
Follow the Camera
and you will find Ron.

1372
02:17:11,426 --> 02:17:13,553
You did your best, Fawkes.

1373
02:17:14,637 --> 02:17:17,098
I was very slow.

1374
02:17:37,869 --> 02:17:39,621
Sure.

1375
02:17:39,871 --> 02:17:42,749
Phoenix tears have
healing powers.

1376
02:17:44,334 --> 02:17:46,169
Thank you.

1377
02:17:47,879 --> 02:17:50,006
It's all right now, Ginny.

1378
02:17:51,174 --> 02:17:53,343
It's over.

1379
02:17:54,344 --> 02:17:56,888
It's just a memory.

1380
02:17:59,807 --> 02:18:05,146
Incredible!
This looks like magic!

1381
02:18:16,407 --> 02:18:19,077
They both realize, naturally...

1382
02:18:19,243 --> 02:18:24,749
...that in the last 12 hours
They violated perhaps a dozen rules.

1383
02:18:25,416 --> 02:18:26,417
Yes, sir.

1384
02:18:26,584 --> 02:18:29,837
There is enough evidence
to expel them.

1385
02:18:30,004 --> 02:18:31,214
Yes, sir.

1386
02:18:31,381 --> 02:18:34,133
Therefore it is appropriate...

1387
02:18:35,677 --> 02:18:37,929
...may they both receive...

1388
02:18:38,429 --> 02:18:42,558
...special prizes
for his services to the school.

1389
02:18:44,602 --> 02:18:46,479
Thank you, sir!

1390
02:18:47,063 --> 02:18:49,357
And now, Mr. Weasley, do me a favor...

1391
02:18:49,524 --> 02:18:53,695
...to send an owl to deliver
these papers to Azkaban.

1392
02:18:54,779 --> 02:18:59,575
We want our return
preserve guard.

1393
02:19:04,539 --> 02:19:08,876
First, I want
Thank you, Harry.

1394
02:19:09,502 --> 02:19:13,006
you must have shown me
great loyalty in the House.

1395
02:19:13,881 --> 02:19:18,428
Only that could do
that Fawkes was with you.

1396
02:19:20,847 --> 02:19:22,390
And...

1397
02:19:22,932 --> 02:19:24,392
"second".

1398
02:19:24,559 --> 02:19:29,313
...I feel like something is bothering you.

1399
02:19:29,564 --> 02:19:32,066
Am I right, Harry?

1400
02:19:33,901 --> 02:19:35,611
The only thing is...

1401
02:19:36,779 --> 02:19:41,534
You see, sir, I couldn't help
noticing certain things...

1402
02:19:41,701 --> 02:19:47,331
...certain similarities
between Tom Riddle and me.

1403
02:19:47,915 --> 02:19:49,125
I see.

1404
02:19:49,292 --> 02:19:55,089
Well, you know how to speak Parseltongue, Harry.
Why?

1405
02:19:55,506 --> 02:20:01,054
Because Lord Voldemort
He knows how to speak Parseltongue.

1406
02:20:02,263 --> 02:20:04,974
If I'm not mistaken, Harry...

1407
02:20:05,391 --> 02:20:09,228
...he transferred some to you
of his powers...

1408
02:20:09,395 --> 02:20:12,315
...the night he gave you that scar.

1409
02:20:12,482 --> 02:20:16,402
Did Voldemort transfer me
some of your powers to me?

1410
02:20:18,321 --> 02:20:20,990
Not on purpose...

1411
02:20:21,908 --> 02:20:23,826
...but yes.

1412
02:20:25,745 --> 02:20:29,040
The hat was right.
I should be in Slytherin.

1413
02:20:29,207 --> 02:20:34,045
It's true. You possess many of the qualities
which Voldemort himself appreciates.

1414
02:20:34,212 --> 02:20:37,090
Determination, ingenuity, and...

1415
02:20:37,256 --> 02:20:41,260
...if you allow me, right
disregard for the rules.

1416
02:20:41,928 --> 02:20:45,932
Why, then, the hat
Did he send you to Gryffindor?

1417
02:20:46,724 --> 02:20:50,436
- Because I asked him to.
- Exactly, Harry. Exact.

1418
02:20:50,603 --> 02:20:52,688
Which differentiates you from Voldemort.

1419
02:20:52,855 --> 02:20:56,692
Our skills are not
what reveals our essence.

1420
02:20:57,026 --> 02:20:59,153
They are our decisions.

1421
02:21:02,824 --> 02:21:06,202
If you want proof that
You belong to Gryffindor...

1422
02:21:06,369 --> 02:21:11,249
...I suggest you watch
this more closely.

1423
02:21:12,250 --> 02:21:13,960
Be careful.

1424
02:21:19,590 --> 02:21:22,260
Godric Gryffindor.

1425
02:21:22,426 --> 02:21:26,556
Yes. Only a true Gryffindor
can take that out of the hat.

1426
02:21:35,398 --> 02:21:36,816
Dobby!

1427
02:21:38,067 --> 02:21:42,446
So this is your master.
You serve the Malfoy family.

1428
02:21:44,657 --> 02:21:47,994
Then we'll settle accounts.

1429
02:21:53,833 --> 02:21:55,418
Don't get in my way, Potter.

1430
02:21:55,585 --> 02:21:59,213
So, it's true. You have returned.

1431
02:21:59,881 --> 02:22:02,633
When the council knew
that Weasley's daughter...

1432
02:22:02,800 --> 02:22:07,013
...was in the Chamber
They thought it appropriate to call me.

1433
02:22:07,847 --> 02:22:11,934
- How ridiculous!
- The curious thing, Lucius, is that...

1434
02:22:12,101 --> 02:22:15,771
...several members had the impression
that you were going to curse them...

1435
02:22:15,938 --> 02:22:18,774
...if they didn't agree to suspend me.

1436
02:22:19,233 --> 02:22:22,695
- How dare you?
- Sorry?

1437
02:22:22,862 --> 02:22:26,616
My only concern always
has been and always will be...

1438
02:22:26,782 --> 02:22:29,619
...the well-being of this school...

1439
02:22:29,785 --> 02:22:34,123
...and of course, from their students.

1440
02:22:38,127 --> 02:22:42,340
Has the culprit been
Identified, I guess?

1441
02:22:42,757 --> 02:22:44,300
Oh, YES.

1442
02:22:45,885 --> 02:22:47,720
And?

1443
02:22:48,888 --> 02:22:50,932
Who was it?

1444
02:22:57,313 --> 02:22:59,899
Voldemort.

1445
02:23:01,025 --> 02:23:06,489
Only this time he decided to act
through someone else...

1446
02:23:07,031 --> 02:23:10,660
...using this.

1447
02:23:13,329 --> 02:23:14,872
I see.

1448
02:23:16,332 --> 02:23:20,544
Fortunately, our young
Mr. Potter found out.

1449
02:23:20,920 --> 02:23:24,590
Let's hope none of the old
Voldemort school supplies...

1450
02:23:24,757 --> 02:23:28,010
...come back
into innocent hands.

1451
02:23:28,344 --> 02:23:32,265
The consequences
For the person responsible they would be...

1452
02:23:32,640 --> 02:23:34,517
...severe.

1453
02:23:35,893 --> 02:23:38,688
Well, let's wait...

1454
02:23:38,854 --> 02:23:44,402
...may Mr. Potter always walk
here to save us.

1455
02:23:45,194 --> 02:23:48,948
Don't worry. I'll be here.

1456
02:23:57,707 --> 02:23:59,709
Dumbledore.

1457
02:24:00,876 --> 02:24:04,380
Come on, Dobby. We're leaving now.

1458
02:24:21,689 --> 02:24:26,110
Sir?
May I have that?

1459
02:24:32,575 --> 02:24:34,160
Mr. Malfoy!

1460
02:24:34,327 --> 02:24:36,537
Mr. Malfoy!

1461
02:24:36,996 --> 02:24:39,165
I have something that belongs to you.

1462
02:24:40,833 --> 02:24:43,753
To me? I don't know what you're talking about.

1463
02:24:44,003 --> 02:24:45,546
I think you do know, sir.

1464
02:24:45,713 --> 02:24:48,799
I think you put the diary
in Ginny's cauldron...

1465
02:24:48,966 --> 02:24:50,426
...that day, in Diagon Alley.

1466
02:24:51,093 --> 02:24:53,637
So you think so?

1467
02:25:01,020 --> 02:25:04,106
Why don't you try it?

1468
02:25:10,321 --> 02:25:12,490
Let's go, Dobby.

1469
02:25:13,783 --> 02:25:15,826
Open it.

1470
02:25:19,372 --> 02:25:20,915
Dobby!

1471
02:25:21,082 --> 02:25:24,251
Master has given Dobby a sock.

1472
02:25:24,502 --> 02:25:26,629
What? I didn't give you...

1473
02:25:26,796 --> 02:25:30,466
Master gave him clothes
to Dobby!

1474
02:25:30,633 --> 02:25:33,719
Dobby is free!

1475
02:25:40,267 --> 02:25:43,979
Because of you I lost my servant!

1476
02:25:50,986 --> 02:25:54,990
It won't hurt Harry Potter!

1477
02:26:07,128 --> 02:26:10,840
Your parents too
They were meddling fools.

1478
02:26:11,006 --> 02:26:14,176
Don't forget my words.
One day soon...

1479
02:26:14,343 --> 02:26:19,515
...you're going to run yourself
unpleasant luck.

1480
02:26:25,229 --> 02:26:31,152
Harry Potter freed Dobby!
How can Dobby repay him?

1481
02:26:31,527 --> 02:26:35,739
- Just promise me one thing.
- Whatever, sir.

1482
02:26:37,700 --> 02:26:40,202
That you won't try again
save my life.

1483
02:26:46,333 --> 02:26:49,336
- Welcome back, Sir Nicholas!
- Thank you!

1484
02:26:49,628 --> 02:26:52,006
- Good evening, Sir Nicholas!
- Good night!

1485
02:26:52,173 --> 02:26:55,050
- How nice it is to see you!
- Thank you!

1486
02:26:56,469 --> 02:26:58,679
Hello!

1487
02:27:00,389 --> 02:27:05,019
- Hermione! Welcome back!
- Thank you, Sir Nicholas.

1488
02:27:08,230 --> 02:27:11,567
Harry! It's Hermione!

1489
02:27:38,427 --> 02:27:42,097
- Welcome back, Hermione.
- I'm glad to be back.

1490
02:27:42,264 --> 02:27:44,892
Congratulations! I can't
believe they resolved this.

1491
02:27:45,059 --> 02:27:47,311
You helped us a lot.

1492
02:27:47,478 --> 02:27:50,731
- Without you, we wouldn't have been able to.
- Thank you.

1493
02:27:52,566 --> 02:27:55,528
' Allow me your attention,
or
please?

1494
02:27:59,657 --> 02:28:02,201
Before starting the banquet...

1495
02:28:02,368 --> 02:28:08,624
...let's give a big round of applause to the teacher
Sprout and Madam Pomfrey...

1496
02:28:08,791 --> 02:28:12,920
...whose mandrake juice
was administered...

1497
02:28:13,087 --> 02:28:15,756
...with success to all
those who were petrified.

1498
02:28:26,267 --> 02:28:29,270
Also, dice
recent events...

1499
02:28:29,436 --> 02:28:31,605
...as a school gift...

1500
02:28:31,772 --> 02:28:35,734
...all exams
have been cancelled.

1501
02:28:56,922 --> 02:28:58,966
Sorry for being late.

1502
02:29:05,014 --> 02:29:09,393
The owl that delivered my papers
He got lost and confused.

1503
02:29:09,727 --> 02:29:13,022
a rare bird
His name is Errol.

1504
02:29:28,829 --> 02:29:34,710
And I just want to say that if there wasn't
been by you, Harry and Ron...

1505
02:29:35,002 --> 02:29:37,921
...and Hermione, of course...

1506
02:29:38,589 --> 02:29:42,718
...I would still be
you know where...

1507
02:29:42,885 --> 02:29:46,430
...so just
I want to tell you: Thank you!

1508
02:29:55,856 --> 02:29:58,776
Hogwarts, without you,
It's not Hogwarts, Hagrid.

1509
02:40:46,047 --> 02:40:51,594
WHO AM I?
